	)
	(text "1.08 Mohm || about 6 pF.  ESD diode ESD701: once a discharge triggers it, it holds at 31 V (typical), so a\nsource of up to 25 V does not keep it on (the PESD30VF1BBL it replaces held at 12 ... 14 V).  100R after it\ndamps the probe lead (at 5 V it would ring the node 0.28 V below ground).  Divider 866k / 215k = 5.03 : 1,\ncompensated 4.7p 0.1pF / 10p 2 % (3.9p leaves it 20 % under-compensated with the\ncomparator's input capacitance).  Clamp: -0.6 V ... VCLAMP + 0.6 V at the node: +/-25 V gives 27 uA.\nComparator: input on -IN, threshold on +IN through 1k; 330k from the output gives 50 mV hysteresis at the probe, 58 ...\n80 mV with the comparator's own.  47p holds the threshold pin against the comparator's 4 pF differential input\ncapacitance, which kicks it on every edge; more would delay the hysteresis (1k x C) and let slow noisy edges chatter.\nThe output is inverted (high = input below threshold): the gateware inverts it.  Test point on this channel's output\nafter the 22R (delay and hysteresis checks: the comparator pin itself is boxed in by the cell's parts); none\non the divider node, where a pad's capacitance would upset the compensation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 264.5 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6bd9fdb4-d722-5ac3-a2ea-a46c4ae6d8b5")
	)
	(text "Pod B probe header (2 x 8, 2.54 mm shrouded and keyed, right angle): signal on odd pins, ground beside it on even pins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "74a0feac-0959-548e-9d85-abf8b69b5957")
	)
	(text "6  Pod B: eight input channels (probe pin -> divider -> comparator)"
